From 869a595e944c8070c3af7477585bdffe4fbd3b9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 21:33:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: the thresholds of DistributionY100nit within
 a scene, measured

DARK_STEP (2) and DARK_BIG_STEP (10) were chosen without a measurement.
They are now measured: what goes out with each picture is replayed
from the measurements of two streams, each picture's measurement taken
one picture late and the first picture of a scene waiting for its own,
as in Kodi, against each scene's ideal computed after the fact from
every pixel in float64 (DistributionY100nit: the average over the
scene's pictures of their percentage at or below 100 cd/m2;
DistributionY99: the highest of their 99.99th percentiles of
luminance). Streams: Cosmos Laundromat (18 192 pictures, the 100
scenes of its Dolby Vision metadata) and the base layer of a profile 7
FEL test stream (2878 pictures, 21 scenes).

Mean |error| of DistributionY100nit in points, and changes of the
packet within a scene per 1000 pictures (Cosmos / FEL):
  step 0     1.694 / 4.135   38.98 / 26.75
  step 1     1.732 / 4.187   37.27 / 21.89
  step 2     1.740 / 4.288   37.21 / 20.85
  never      1.745 / 4.293   37.21 / 20.85
  every move, no interval   1.639 / 3.903   68.72 / 64.28
Step 2 is on the Pareto front of both: it adds no change of its own to
those the other values make, with a lower error than never; the
criterion is the fewest changes among the variants whose mean error is
within half a step of the InfoFrame (0.5 point) of the best, and among
those the lowest error. DARK_BIG_STEP makes no difference from 8 up on
either stream, from 3 up on the second: 10 is kept. The values do not
change; the comment says what they are measured on.

DistributionY99 keeps the steps of the other luminances (32 and 64 in
PQ): by the same criterion 32 and 96 would change the packet 3.8 %
less often on Cosmos (35.79 against 37.21 per 1000) for 0.9 % more
error (20.24 against 20.07 codes), and nothing on the FEL stream: not
a clear gain. The error that remains in both values is that of a
scene not yet seen whole (with every move sent, 1.64 / 3.90 points and
19.57 / 4.82 codes), which a player that does not look ahead cannot
avoid. The level 1 maximum of the RPU in place of the measurement is
far off (107 / 71 codes).
---
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_dvplus.c | 17 +++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_dvplus.c b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_dvplus.c
index 6866e78..3406cd9 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_dvplus.c
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_dvplus.c
@@ -26,8 +26,21 @@ const struct dvbridge_dvplus_params dvbridge_dvplus_default_params = {
 
 /* (version 1: DistributionY100nit is a percentage, not a luminance; within a scene a move of it by more than DARK_STEP
  * points counts as a move, by more than DARK_BIG_STEP as one that may change what is sent at any time, as pq_step and
- * big_step do for a luminance. Chosen, not measured on the bench of the others: what a display does with this place
- * is not known) */
+ * big_step do for a luminance; DistributionY99 is a luminance and moves by pq_step and big_step as the others.
+ * Measured (2026-11-03) by replaying what goes out picture by picture, each picture's measurement taken one picture
+ * late and the first of a scene waiting for its own, against each scene's ideal computed after the fact from every
+ * pixel in float64: Cosmos Laundromat (18 192 pictures, the 100 scenes of its Dolby Vision metadata) and the base
+ * layer of a profile 7 FEL stream (2878 pictures, 21 scenes). Mean |error| of DistributionY100nit in points and
+ * changes of the packet within a scene per 1000 pictures, Cosmos / FEL:
+ *   step 0: 1.694 / 4.135 at 38.98 / 26.75; step 1: 1.732 / 4.187 at 37.27 / 21.89; step 2: 1.740 / 4.288 at
+ *   37.21 / 20.85; never: 1.745 / 4.293 at 37.21 / 20.85; every move sent, no interval: 1.639 / 3.903 at 68.72 / 64.28.
+ * Step 2 adds no change of its own to what the other values already change, with a lower error than never: the
+ * fewest changes, and the lowest error among those (an error within half a step of the InfoFrame of the best).
+ * DARK_BIG_STEP makes no difference from 8 up on either stream (from 3 up on the second): 10 is kept for a scene
+ * whose first pictures are unlike the rest. The error that remains is that of a scene not yet seen whole, which a
+ * player that does not look ahead cannot have: 1.64 / 3.90 points with every move sent. For DistributionY99 the
+ * shared steps are kept: 32 / 96 would change the packet 3.8 % less often on Cosmos for 0.9 % more error, and nothing
+ * on the second stream; not a clear gain.) */
 #define DARK_STEP 2
 #define DARK_BIG_STEP 10
 
-- 
2.53.0

